    "title": "What channel is Kansas vs St. John's on today? Time, TV schedule for March Madness game",
    "text": "March 22, 2026, 4:07 a.m. CTSAN DIEGO, California — Kansas basketball’s men’s NCAA tournament run continues Sunday with a game in the round of 32 against St. John’s.The Jayhawks (24-10) are the No. 4 seed in the East Region, while the Red Storm (29-6) are the No. 5 seed. KU found a way to win against No. 13 seed California Baptist to get to this point, while St. John’s crushed No. 12 seed Northern Iowa. The winner advances to the Sweet 16.Here’s how fans can follow along with this matchup, with tip-off set for 4:15 p.m. (CT) in San Diego, California.What channel is Kansas basketball vs St. John’s game on today?TV channel: CBSLivestream: FuboKansas basketball’s game against St. John’s will be broadcast on CBS during the 2025-26 season. Streaming options include Fubo. Whichever team wins will be facing either No. 1 seed Duke or No. 9 seed TCU in the next round.Kansas basketball vs St. John’s time todayDate: Sunday, March 22Start time: 4:15 p.m. (CT)Kansas basketball will play St. John’s at 4:15 p.m. (CT) in San Diego, California.Watch Kansas basketball in March MadnessKansas basketball vs St. John’s score predictionKansas is the better seed, but St. John’s is entering with far more momentum than the Jayhawks right now. That’s not just with what’s happened so far in the NCAA tournament, but dating back to the end of the regular season and each side’s respective conference tournaments — KU in the Big 12 Conference, St. John’s in the Big East Conference. Look for St. John’s to come away with a 71-66 win.Kansas basketball 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at Kansas’ last three games:March 12 (neutral): TCU — Kansas won 78-73March 13 (neutral): Houston — Kansas lost 69-47March 20 (neutral): California Baptist — Kansas won 68-60St. John’s basketball 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at St. John’s last three games:March 13 (neutral): Seton Hall — St. John’s won 78-68March 14 (neutral): UConn — St. John’s won 72-52March 20 (neutral): Northern Iowa — St. John’s won 79-53Jordan Guskey covers University of Kansas Athletics at The Topeka Capital-Journal. He was the 2022 National Sports Media Association’s sportswriter of the year for the state of Kansas. Contact him at jmguskey@gannett.com or on Twitter at @JordanGuskey.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
